# R-16 fix (22 Sep 2026): this file did not exist, so every contributor's own
# core.autocrlf setting decided line endings on checkout/commit — on a
# Windows dev machine that is usually true, but nothing in the repo enforced
# it, so a contributor on a different default could silently reintroduce
# mixed line endings. `text=auto` lets git normalise text files to LF in the
# repo and check them out using each platform's own convention; binaries are
# marked explicitly so git never tries to diff or normalise them.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
